TITLE:: RightCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that moves selected notes right by a beat subdivision.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/LeftCommand, Classes/SnapCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::RightCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::right:: that moves each selected note right by a beat subdivision. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::.

CODE::resolution:: is a positive integer from 1 to 16, the same fractions of a beat as LINK::Classes/SnapCommand::. The step size is CODE::1.0 / resolution:: beats:
LIST::
## CODE::1::: Whole beat (1.0 beat)
## CODE::2::: Half beat (0.5 beats)
## CODE::4::: Quarter beat (0.25 beats)
## CODE::8::: Eighth beat (0.125 beats)
## CODE::16::: Sixteenth beat (0.0625 beats)
::

A note already on that grid moves one step right. A note off the grid moves to the adjacent grid line to the right. Duration is preserved. LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-nudgeRight:: repositions the note view.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::RightCommand::. Takes no arguments; movement is applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::RightCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Moves each note in CODE::\selectedNotes:: right by the grid implied by CODE::\resolution::.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::nudgeRight::) and CODE::\resolution:: (an LINK::Classes/Integer:: from 1 to 16).

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var note = PianoRollNote(1.0, 60, 100,
	viewFunc: { View() },
	selectFunc: {},
	deselectFunc: {},
	setPart1Func: {},
	setPart2Func: {},
	setPart3Func: {},
	setPart4Func: {},
	moveFunc: { |view, start, stop| ("Moved to " ++ start ++ ".." ++ stop).postln; }
);
note.stop(2.0);

// Move right by a quarter beat (resolution = 4)
RightCommand.new.execute((
	selectedNotes: [note],
	resolution: 4
));
)
::
